 P4.7 retry-2 is reviewed accepted: all three prior-failure probes, 20 focused cases and 64 full production cases pass without skips/flakes/errors. Independent 317 root/candidate hashes and fourteen preserved hashes match; all 27 captures inspected. Final hashed review: docs/perf/phase-four/p4-7-final-review.json. Verify passes 396 plus two expected diagnostics in 44 files. Desktop navigation long task 265 ms exceeds the later 50 ms target; P4.9 remains open. P4.8 adds the currently disabled objects list and integrated accessibility. No final phase acceptance or physical phone throughput is claimed.
+
+P4.7 is committed locally as 4927fc3. P4.8 adds a cold public getObjectsInView query: immutable id/name/kind catalog records, reusable homogeneous projection and membership buffers, stable array identity until contents change. It includes enabled rendered mesh/point centers inside the last camera clip volume, independently of label collision, relevance and occlusion; rejects invalid, behind-camera, disabled, unrendered, not-ready and disposed states. No frame-loop, provider, physical model or asset changes. The nonmodal selectable text list stays open during camera gestures and exposes truthful center/occlusion copy. O opens it; Settings remains the visible action. The shared selection command path and actual trigger focus return are retained.
+
+The list mounts one cold subscription to the existing perf store bridge, releases it on close/unmount, and notifies React only when ID/name/kind membership changes. It adds no independent timer, clock or engine-frame listener. Unified page shortcut policy yields to open dialogs/popovers, text/editable/interactive/card targets, prevented events, IME/229 and browser modifiers. Question mark opens help and both shortcut-opened panels restore their actual canvas/page trigger. Canvas arrows/zoom retain engine ownership, with composition/default/modifier guards added to Input.
+
+P4.8 pins test-only @axe-core/playwright4.13.0/axe-core4.13.0 (MPL-2.0) without changing runtime dependencies or the production allowlist. Seven actual states at desktop/phone widths retain all raw axe results including incomplete rules. Integrated keyboard flows, native Space/Enter/Backspace, list camera/layer/collision/empty/cleanup and focus checks are required. A Profiler wraps the complete Explore subtree, including portals/card/list. Separate isolated Next --profile validation proves callbacks active before two 30-second 1day/sec windows and also retains the original lab profile. Normal production response/budget evidence is kept separate. Short verify passes411 plus2 expected diagnostics/47files; initial directive placement failure is preserved. Production validation is pending, so P4.8 is unaccepted and final P4.9 gates remain open.
+
+P4.8 bridge audit also finds that recurring clock UTC snapshots and perf snapshots could independently schedule 4 Hz React work. The existing clock listener now writes clock text directly and publishes only changed mode/rate/boundary state immediately. The existing perf listener publishes UTC/date and perf together in one store update. Cold explicit time commands remain immediate; the retained clamp helper still covers missed transient boundary flags. No timer or engine frame subscription is added. The new complete-subtree profiling checks and all prior UTC/history/clamp cases must validate this cadence change before acceptance.
